PUBLIC RESPONSE: {A}

The NI 45-106 tests (Ontario, Jan 2021) are clear: an LP qualifies only if (i) it itself shows ≥$5 M net assets on financial statements or (ii) every partner (limited + general) is itself an AI. The three limited partners individually qualify, but the sole GP is a corporation whose share register/ownership is never disclosed (only “gifts” of cash are mentioned). Without that, the “all interest-holders are AIs” route fails, and no entity-level financials are supplied either.  

B meets the combined spousal-income test (> $300 k in each of 2019-2020 + continuation). C meets the spousal net-asset test (= $5 M). D and E both meet the entity net-asset test (D via the $10 M transfer; E via $5.2 M net after the GIC-liability adjustment). Thus A is the sole structure that cannot be confirmed as an AI on the facts given.}

