5.text:
PUBLIC RESPONSE: {A

The NI 45-106 definition (Ontario, Jan 2021) for an LP requires either (i) the LP itself showing ≥$5 M net assets on its most recent financial statements or (ii) every partner (limited + general) itself being an AI. No LP-level financials are supplied, the three limited partners qualify individually, but the sole GP (2538901 Ontario Inc.) is an undescribed corporation whose ownership, shareholders, and financial status are never disclosed. Therefore neither route is satisfied and A fails.

B meets the combined-spousal-income test ($320 k / $350 k both years + continuation). C meets the spousal net-asset test (= $5 M). D meets the entity net-asset test (≥$10 M transferred). E meets the entity net-asset test ($5.2 M after liabilities). The objections on B and E misapply the tests; only A is non-qualifying on the facts.}

